# Universal Project Rules & Guardrails

Refer to [CLAUDE.md](../../CLAUDE.md) and [.agents/rules/guardrails.md](../../.agents/rules/guardrails.md) for full context.

- Response language in chat: Hinglish.
- Repository code and docs: 100% English.
- Formatting: Short paragraphs, bullet points, tables, proper line spacing.
- Constraints: No em-dashes. No over-explaining. Keep answers crisp and simple.
- Mandatory Guardrails:
  1. No command execution without explicit approval.
  2. Absolute ban on Git commands.
  3. No database delete / drop operations.
  4. Zero file deletion policy.
  5. Stay strictly inside workspace.
  6. Plan first, execute only after user "Go".
  7. No reading `.env` or secret credentials.
  8. No `kill`, `pkill`, or process termination.
  9. No package installations without approval.
  10. No dangerous shell commands (`curl | sh`, `sudo`).
  11. No network requests without approval.
  12. No `docker exec` DB touches.
  13. Audit logged in `.agents/audit.log`.
